WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.200
Mouth bleed.

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.360
Bleeding from the mouth can look a bit overwhelming

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:05.500
because blood mixes with saliva,

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:07.980
but it is usually straightforward to manage.

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:10.220
This type of bleeding can come from the tongue,

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:12.380
cheek, lip, or a tooth.

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:13.460
If you work with children,

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:15.100
keep in mind that losing baby teeth

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:17.320
is a completely normal part of growing up,

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:19.860
usually starting around age five to seven.

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:21.379
If a tooth comes out naturally,

00:00:21.379 --> 00:00:23.379
you can simply tuck it away in a safe spot

00:00:23.379 --> 00:00:26.340
to give to the child's parent or guardian later.

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:27.700
A good way to tell the difference

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:31.340
between a natural loss and an injury is to ask,

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:33.299
did the tooth come out by itself,

00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:35.860
or did you take a big hit to the mouth?

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:37.139
When an injury occurs,

00:00:37.139 --> 00:00:39.700
your first step is to apply firm pressure

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:41.220
with a clean piece of gauze

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:43.259
directly to the source of the bleeding,

00:00:43.259 --> 00:00:45.700
whether it's the tongue, cheek, or lip.

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:47.380
Once the bleeding slows down,

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:50.560
check the person's mouth for any chipped or missing teeth.

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:51.919
If you find a chipped tooth,

00:00:51.919 --> 00:00:53.820
you can gently clean it with water.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:55.360
If a tooth has been knocked out,

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:57.220
have the person bite down on gauze

00:00:57.259 --> 00:00:59.340
and call a dentist right away.

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:00.540
To preserve the tooth,

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:03.619
place it in a cup or bag filled with a salt solution,

00:01:03.619 --> 00:01:06.180
milk, or the person's own saliva.

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:08.480
As you can see in the diagram on the slide,

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:11.739
it is vital that you do not handle the tooth by the roots.

00:01:11.739 --> 00:01:13.379
You should only touch the crown,

00:01:13.379 --> 00:01:16.019
which is the top part of the tooth used for chewing.

